  "raw": " substance that caused her to lose consciousness\n\nMother-of-nine who put an 81-year-old into a coma by pouring anti-depressants into a cup of tea at hospital then gave her paracetamol has been spared jail.\n\nJulia Knight, 56, appeared in court today for sentencing at Oxford Crown Court and faces 11 years in prison after she admitted attempting to murder Irene Robson at Horton Hospital in Banbury in October 2014.\n\nThe court was told Knight had been taking paracetamol tablets that she had bought from her local Boots store and, believing to be taking them for her backache, had been injecting herself with them over time.\n\nProsecutor Stephen Jennings said the elderly victim had previously had dementia before undergoing treatment at the hospital.\n\nHe told the court: 'The defendant had the victim placed into bed so that she could pour the tablets into a tea cup.\n\n'She poured the tablet-infused tea",
  "serialized": "substance that caused her to lose consciousness Mother-of-nine who put an 81-year-old into a coma by pouring anti-depressants into a cup of tea at hospital then gave her paracetamol has been spared jail. Julia Knight, 56, appeared in court today for sentencing at Oxford Crown Court and faces 11 years in prison after she admitted attempting to murder Irene Robson at Horton Hospital in Banbury in October 2014. The court was told Knight had been taking paracetamol tablets that she had bought from her local Boots store and, believing to be taking them for her backache, had been injecting herself with them over time. Prosecutor Stephen Jennings said the elderly victim had previously had dementia before undergoing treatment at the hospital. He told the court: 'The defendant had the victim placed into bed so that she could pour the tablets into a tea cup. 'She poured the tablet-infused tea",
